.TH "PERCH-GC" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-gc \- remove orphan blobs, old dead letters, and S3 tombstones
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch gc [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Remove orphaned local blobs, dead letters older than \-\-dead\-letter\-age, enforce the S3 spool limit, and optionally delete S3 objects for deleted messages. An incremental vacuum runs by default.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
\-\-s3\-delete is ignored in SQLite mode.
.IP \(bu 2
Without \-\-s3\-delete, S3 tombstones accumulate.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
report what would be removed
.TP
.B \-\-s3\-delete
delete S3 objects for deleted messages
.TP
.B \-\-dead\-letter\-age <value>
delete dead letters older than this (default: 720h0m0s)
.TP
.B \-\-vacuum
run incremental vacuum after cleanup
.TP
.B \-\-spool
enforce storage.s3.spool_max_bytes
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch gc \-\-config /etc/perch/perch.yaml \-\-dry\-run

perch gc \-\-config /etc/perch/perch.yaml \-\-s3\-delete
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1)
